  "summary": "The red-billed buffalo weaver (Bubalornis niger) is a species of bird in the family Ploceidae. It is found in eastern and southern Africa. Its natural habitat is the dry savanna.",
  "appearance": {
    "description": "The body length of full grown red-billed buffalo weavers is 21 to 25 cm (8.3 to 9.8 in) and body mass averages 82.1 g (2.90 oz) in males and 70.7 g (2.49 oz) in females. This may the largest of the Ploceidae (weaver birds). Visually the sexes are not greatly differentiated from one another.",
    "colors": "The red-billed buffalo weaver (Bubalornis niger) is a species of bird in the family Ploceidae. The body length of full grown red-billed buffalo weavers is 21 to 25 cm (8.3 to 9.8 in) and body mass averages 82.1 g (2.90 oz) in males and 70.7 g (2.49 oz) in females.",
    "wings": "The front wing edges and the wing tips are flecked with white. The female's body is also colored dark chocolate brown, without the white flecks on the wings."
